2. Definitions

"Licensor" means RR — GEL RAM Project, or the person or legal entity that validly succeeds to the relevant rights.

"You" means any individual, sole trader, partnership, company, organization, or other legal entity exercising rights under this license.

"Software" means the GEL RAM source code, documentation, demonstration media, build material and other files to which a distribution expressly applies this license, excluding Third-Party Material.

"Third-Party Material" means material identified as owned or licensed by another party. Third-Party Material remains subject to its own license terms and is not relicensed by this license.

"Modification" means any change to, adaptation of, derivative work based on, or work containing modified portions of the Software.

"Noncommercial Purpose" means use that does not generate, enable, support, or form part of a Monetized Use.

"Monetized Use" means use of the Software or a Modification, other than permitted Evaluation, that directly or indirectly receives, earns, enables, supports, protects, or is intended to produce money or other material financial benefit for You or another person. It includes, without limitation: sale or licensing of a product; paid subscriptions; SaaS or hosted services; advertising-supported services; sponsorship tied to access or operation; paid consulting or contract work; customer-facing production systems; deployment in revenue-generating infrastructure; and production use that materially reduces the operating cost of a commercial activity.

Donations, tips, crowdfunding, sponsorships, or similar payments received specifically because of a GEL RAM-based activity are Monetized Use when they fund, reward, or support that activity. An unrelated personal gift that is not connected to GEL RAM use is outside this definition.

"Evaluation" means testing, benchmarking, studying, prototyping, modifying, or integrating the Software or a Modification in a non-production environment solely to assess, learn about, validate, or decide whether to obtain commercial rights. Evaluation may be performed by any person or organization, including a for-profit entity, and has no fixed time limit under this public license. Evaluation does not include customer-facing deployment, production operation, paid service delivery, sale, subscription use, advertising-supported operation, billable work, use of GEL RAM to train or tune a production system, generation of deliverables for a paying customer, or use of the Software or a Modification to operate or materially improve a revenue-generating service or product. Evaluating GEL RAM solely to decide whether to obtain commercial rights is permitted even when the evaluator is a for-profit entity.

"Commercial Agreement" means a separate written agreement signed by the Licensor and the person or entity receiving commercial rights.

"Commercial Improvement" means a Modification, extension, optimization, integration layer, or other GEL RAM-derived improvement created or used for a Monetized Use, excluding independent components that merely communicate with GEL RAM through a documented interface without incorporating or adapting GEL RAM code.

3. Noncommercial License

Subject to this license, the Licensor grants You a worldwide, non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable, royalty-free copyright license to reproduce, run, study, modify, and share the Software for Noncommercial Purposes.

You may keep Noncommercial Modifications private without a time limit. You are not required to publish private Noncommercial Modifications merely because You created, ran, maintained, or improved them.

You may share the Software or a Modification with other people for Noncommercial Purposes, including private sharing, research collaboration, teaching, hobby work, community experimentation, and noncommercial redistribution of demonstration media, provided You preserve this license and the notices required by section 8.

4. Free Evaluation

Any person or organization may evaluate the Software and may create Evaluation Modifications without payment and without a fixed evaluation deadline.

Evaluation may use ordinary rented or owned computing infrastructure, but the Software or a Modification may not be deployed as part of a paid plan, customer-facing production environment, revenue-generating service, or other Monetized Use under this section.

Evaluation does not grant commercial rights. If Evaluation becomes a Monetized Use, commercial rights are required before that Monetized Use begins.

5. Monetized and Commercial Use

No Monetized Use is licensed by these public terms.

Before beginning a Monetized Use, You must obtain a Commercial Agreement from the Licensor. This rule applies regardless of whether You are an individual, freelancer, sole trader, nonprofit, company, or other organization.

Creating Your own Modification does not remove this requirement when that Modification incorporates, adapts, derives from, or materially uses the Software.

Publishing source code, giving away a copy, paying infrastructure costs, or calling a deployment an experiment does not convert a Monetized Use into a Noncommercial Purpose.

6. Commercial Reciprocity and Closed Modifications

A Commercial Agreement must define the applicable payment model, which may include a subscription, fixed fee, usage fee, revenue share, royalty, or another written arrangement.

The Licensor may offer a reciprocal commercial option in which the commercial user pays the agreed amount and provides agreed Commercial Improvements or their Corresponding Source to the Licensor and, where the Commercial Agreement requires it, to the GEL RAM community.

The Licensor may also offer a closed-modification commercial option under which agreed Commercial Improvements may remain private. Closed commercial rights exist only when the Commercial Agreement expressly grants them and may require a higher fee, subscription tier, royalty, revenue share, or other compensation.

No person obtains a right to keep Monetized GEL RAM-derived Modifications closed merely by paying an unsolicited amount, publishing some source, or using the Software privately before commercialization.

A Commercial Agreement may condition access to future releases, extensions, modules, updates, support, or closed-modification rights on an active subscription or other continuing payment. Rights to previously supplied versions and post-termination obligations are governed only by that Commercial Agreement.

7. Independent Components

Separate, independently developed components may remain under their own terms if they do not incorporate or adapt protected GEL RAM code. Mere communication with GEL RAM through an API, file format, process boundary, or protocol does not by itself make an independent component a Modification.

Moving GEL RAM-derived code into a plugin, wrapper, service, generated file, encoded payload, or separate process does not by itself make that code independent.

